MID_TUT_Root_AnimalDeployment_t: Mounts
MID_TUT_Root_AnimalDeployment_m01_001: {SetColor=Gold}Assigning {SetColor=Default}a captured {SetColor=Gold}mount{SetColor=Default} from Assign in the\nInventory menu will {SetColor=Gold}increase a unit's stats{SetColor=Default}.
MID_TUT_Root_AnimalDeployment_m01_002: {SetColor=Gold}Fighting while a mount is assigned{SetColor=Default} will\nraise the unit and mount's {SetColor=Gold}Bond Lv{SetColor=Default},\nwhich may {SetColor=Gold}teach an ability{SetColor=Default}.
MID_TUT_AutoSave_t: Autosave
MID_TUT_AutoSave_m01_001: Your progress is {SetColor=Gold}saved automatically{SetColor=Default}. When you see\nthe {SetColor=Gold}save icon{SetColor=Default} at the bottom right of the screen,\ndo not {SetColor=Gold}turn off the console's power{SetColor=Default} while it displays.
MID_TUT_AutoSave_m01_002: 
MID_TUT_Mouse1_t: Mouse Controls
MID_TUT_Mouse1_m01_001: {SetColor=Gold}All unit actions and commands{SetColor=Default} can be\naccomplished using {SetColor=Gold}mouse controls{SetColor=Default}.
MID_TUT_Mouse1_m01_002: You can {SetColor=Gold}change {SetColor=Default}to {SetColor=Gold}mouse controls {SetColor=Default}by {SetColor=Gold}standing{SetColor=Default}\nthe {SetColor=Gold}Joy-Con 2 (R) {SetColor=Default}controller {SetColor=Menu}up on a flat surface.{SetColor=Default}
MID_TUT_Mouse2_t: Mouse Control Details
MID_TUT_Mouse2_m01_001: How the mouse controls work depends\non the situation. You can check specific\nusage from {SetColor=Gold}Mouse Controls {SetColor=Default}in {SetColor=Gold}System{SetColor=Default}.
MID_TUT_Mouse2_m01_002: {SetColor=Gold}Press {ButtonPlus} {SetColor=Default}on the explanation screen to {SetColor=Gold}reset the \nangle calibration for mouse controls{SetColor=Default}. If you find\nthe cursor difficult to control, try {SetColor=Gold}recalibrating{SetColor=Default}.
MID_TUT_Mouse2_m01_003: Some {SetColor=Gold}button functions {SetColor=Default}will {SetColor=Gold}change {SetColor=Default}when you're using\nmouse controls. Check the {SetColor=Gold}button help {SetColor=Default}display.
MID_TUT_Mouse2_m01_004: You can check the current {SetColor=Gold}{Lowercase}Mouse Controls{NormalCase}{SetColor=Default}\nby {SetColor=Gold}pressing {ButtonPlus} while using mouse controls{SetColor=Default}.
